    <statement><p>Let <m>\displaystyle f(x)= \frac{8 \sin x}{4 \sin x + 6 \cos x}</m>.</p>
<p>Then <m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
<p>The equation of the tangent line to <m>y=f(x)</m> at <m>a = \pi/4</m> can be written in the form <m>y=mx+b</m> where</p>
<p><m>m =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> and</p>
<p><m>b =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{8\cdot 6}{\left(4\sin\mathopen{}\left(x\right)+6\cos\mathopen{}\left(x\right)\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
